  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\nIssued at 1223 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nA 594 dm upper-level ridge axis is centered over portions of the\nSouthern Plains and Lower Mississippi Valley. This upper-level\nridge continues to bring a continuation of very hot temperatures\nand persistent dry weather to the Mid-South. Late morning\ntemperatures range from the upper 80s to lower 90s with surface\ndewpoints in the 60s.\n\nThe aforementioned upper-level ridge will continue to bring very\nhot temperatures and dry weather to the area through the\nremainder of the weekend. Heat index values over the past couple\nof days have struggled to reach 105 degrees as drier air has\nmixed down to the surface with afternoon temperatures rising into\nthe upper 90s to around 100 degrees. Confidence remains low for\nsites reaching Heat Advisory criteria this afternoon.\nConsequently, the current Heat Advisory may be cancelled early\nrather than extending into Sunday if current short-term trends\npersist.\n\nMid to long range model ensemble and deterministic solutions\nindicate the upper-level ridge will weaken slightly by early next\nweek. Shower and thunderstorm chances are anticipated to return\nto some locations Monday night into Tuesday as a weak cold front\ndrops into the region. This front is not expected to bring any\nappreciable rainfall with LREF probabilities of rainfall greater\nthan one-tenth of an inch remaining at or below 10 percent.\nTemperatures behind this front are still anticipated to remain\nabove normal with LREF/NBM probabilities of temperatures\n90 degrees or warmer dropping down to 30 percent for mid to late\nnext week.",
